    {
      "id": "856ca19e-137b-4fc2-a36a-019f245f4b9e",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 1,
      "content": "Articulation Agreement Overview This agreement outlines lower-division course requirements specific to the major. Students are strongly encouraged to consult an academic advisor to ensure they meet all degree requirements for their intended baccalaureate program. Helpful Resources: CSUB Catalog Transfer Admission Requirements Academic Advising Student Centers CSUB Program Pathways Mapper Course Equivalency Information for 4-Year Institutions Students and staff can explore course transfer equivalencies through the Transfer Evaluation System (TES) . Equivalency agreements are updated regularly and subject to change. For the most current information, please refer to TES or contact the Articulation Office .",
      "contentHtml": "<p><strong>Articulation&nbsp;Agreement&nbsp;Overview</strong></p><p>This&nbsp;agreement&nbsp;outlines&nbsp;lower-division&nbsp;course&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;specific&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;major.&nbsp;Students&nbsp;are&nbsp;strongly&nbsp;encouraged&nbsp;to&nbsp;consult&nbsp;an&nbsp;academic&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;to&nbsp;ensure&nbsp;they&nbsp;meet&nbsp;all&nbsp;degree&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;for&nbsp;their&nbsp;intended&nbsp;baccalaureate&nbsp;program.</p><p></p><p><strong>Helpful&nbsp;Resources:</strong></p><ul><li><a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB&nbsp;Catalog</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/admissions/transfer\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer&nbsp;Admission&nbsp;Requirements</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/advising\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Academic&nbsp;Advising&nbsp;Student&nbsp;Centers</a></li><li><a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/ppm\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">CSUB&nbsp;Program&nbsp;Pathways&nbsp;Mapper</a></li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Course&nbsp;Equivalency&nbsp;Information&nbsp;for&nbsp;4-Year&nbsp;Institutions</strong></p><p>Students&nbsp;and&nbsp;staff&nbsp;can&nbsp;explore&nbsp;course&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;equivalencies&nbsp;through&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://tes.collegesource.com/publicview/TES_publicview01.aspx?rid=7ea49506-39bf-4815-8199-734369e7a30c&amp;aid=ccc830a2-2435-4dd6-b352-a586b4575654\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Transfer&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;System&nbsp;(TES)</a>.&nbsp;Equivalency&nbsp;agreements&nbsp;are&nbsp;updated&nbsp;regularly&nbsp;and&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;change.&nbsp;For&nbsp;the&nbsp;most&nbsp;current&nbsp;information,&nbsp;please&nbsp;refer&nbsp;to&nbsp;TES&nbsp;or&nbsp;contact&nbsp;the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/articulation/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Articulation&nbsp;Office</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "40c6abe2-94f6-4440-82f4-019f245f4b9e",
      "type": "GeneralTitle",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 2,
      "content": "About the Major",
      "contentHtml": null
    },
    {
      "id": "a7db2926-9546-4ef5-8f69-019f245f4b9e",
      "type": "GeneralText",
      "area": "General",
      "position": 3,
      "content": "The Department of Public Policy and Administration at CSU Bakersfield will foster and enhance critical thinking, communication, management, a public service perspective, and engagement in the policy process among present and future managers in government, nonprofit, and healthcare organizations within the San Joaquin Valley. The critical skills learned from this curriculum will ensure that managers in the government, nonprofit, and healthcare sectors exercise governance in an inclusive and socially responsible manner. Strategic Goals The purpose of the PPA programs is to prepare competent, ethical, and effective public, nonprofit, and healthcare managers and leaders to advance the public service. Consistent with, and in addition to, established university academic performance and student conduct standards for undergraduates, those admitted, retained, and awarded degrees must possess and demonstrate academic and professional integrity in all activities to inspire public confidence and trust in public service. Students and applicants who violate academic integrity or professional ethical standards of behavior will be subject to the academic integrity procedures of the university. Such actions are, of course, subject to university review and appeal. Undergraduate students without experience in public service or administration are required to complete a service-learning requirement. For additional information, visit the following: Department of Public Policy and Administration Program Requirements - Public Administration, BA",
      "contentHtml": "<p>The&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Public&nbsp;Policy&nbsp;and&nbsp;Administration&nbsp;at&nbsp;CSU&nbsp;Bakersfield&nbsp;will&nbsp;foster&nbsp;and&nbsp;enhance&nbsp;critical&nbsp;thinking,&nbsp;communication,&nbsp;management,&nbsp;a&nbsp;public&nbsp;service&nbsp;perspective,&nbsp;and&nbsp;engagement&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;policy&nbsp;process&nbsp;among&nbsp;present&nbsp;and&nbsp;future&nbsp;managers&nbsp;in&nbsp;government,&nbsp;nonprofit,&nbsp;and&nbsp;healthcare&nbsp;organizations&nbsp;within&nbsp;the&nbsp;San&nbsp;Joaquin&nbsp;Valley.&nbsp;The&nbsp;critical&nbsp;skills&nbsp;learned&nbsp;from&nbsp;this&nbsp;curriculum&nbsp;will&nbsp;ensure&nbsp;that&nbsp;managers&nbsp;in&nbsp;the&nbsp;government,&nbsp;nonprofit,&nbsp;and&nbsp;healthcare&nbsp;sectors&nbsp;exercise&nbsp;governance&nbsp;in&nbsp;an&nbsp;inclusive&nbsp;and&nbsp;socially&nbsp;responsible&nbsp;manner.</p><p></p><p>Strategic&nbsp;Goals</p><ol><li>The&nbsp;purpose&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;PPA&nbsp;programs&nbsp;is&nbsp;to&nbsp;prepare&nbsp;competent,&nbsp;ethical,&nbsp;and&nbsp;effective&nbsp;public,&nbsp;nonprofit,&nbsp;and&nbsp;healthcare&nbsp;managers&nbsp;and&nbsp;leaders&nbsp;to&nbsp;advance&nbsp;the&nbsp;public&nbsp;service.</li><li>Consistent&nbsp;with,&nbsp;and&nbsp;in&nbsp;addition&nbsp;to,&nbsp;established&nbsp;university&nbsp;academic&nbsp;performance&nbsp;and&nbsp;student&nbsp;conduct&nbsp;standards&nbsp;for&nbsp;undergraduates,&nbsp;those&nbsp;admitted,&nbsp;retained,&nbsp;and&nbsp;awarded&nbsp;degrees&nbsp;must&nbsp;possess&nbsp;and&nbsp;demonstrate&nbsp;academic&nbsp;and&nbsp;professional&nbsp;integrity&nbsp;in&nbsp;all&nbsp;activities&nbsp;to&nbsp;inspire&nbsp;public&nbsp;confidence&nbsp;and&nbsp;trust&nbsp;in&nbsp;public&nbsp;service.&nbsp;Students&nbsp;and&nbsp;applicants&nbsp;who&nbsp;violate&nbsp;academic&nbsp;integrity&nbsp;or&nbsp;professional&nbsp;ethical&nbsp;standards&nbsp;of&nbsp;behavior&nbsp;will&nbsp;be&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;academic&nbsp;integrity&nbsp;procedures&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;university.&nbsp;Such&nbsp;actions&nbsp;are,&nbsp;of&nbsp;course,&nbsp;subject&nbsp;to&nbsp;university&nbsp;review&nbsp;and&nbsp;appeal.</li><li>Undergraduate&nbsp;students&nbsp;without&nbsp;experience&nbsp;in&nbsp;public&nbsp;service&nbsp;or&nbsp;administration&nbsp;are&nbsp;required&nbsp;to&nbsp;complete&nbsp;a&nbsp;service-learning&nbsp;requirement.</li></ol><p></p><p>For&nbsp;additional&nbsp;information,&nbsp;visit&nbsp;the&nbsp;following:</p><p>Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.csub.edu/bpa/public-policy-and-administration\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Public&nbsp;Policy&nbsp;and&nbsp;Administration</a></p><p>Program&nbsp;Requirements&nbsp;-&nbsp;<a href=\"https://catalog.csub.edu/academic-degrees-programs/undergraduate-majors/public-administration-ba/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Public&nbsp;Administration,&nbsp;BA</a></p>"
    }
